2. scrcpy (adapted code)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product includes code adapted from scrcpy (https://github.com/Genymobile/scrcpy):

  probes/android/velocity-tree-server/src/com/velocity/tree/VideoServer.java
  (compiled into crates/velocity-android/assets/velocity-tree.jar, which is
  embedded in the velocity binary)
    The screen capture and H.264 streaming design (a DisplayManager virtual
    display or SurfaceControl display mirroring the screen onto a MediaCodec
    input surface, the encoder format keys, the size fallbacks, and the
    12-byte packet header with config/key-frame flags and the session
    packet), adapted from scrcpy's server
    (server/src/main/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/: video/SurfaceEncoder.java,
    video/ScreenCapture.java, device/Streamer.java,
    wrappers/DisplayManager.java, wrappers/SurfaceControl.java).
    Copyright (C) 2018 Genymobile
    Copyright (C) 2018-2025 Romain Vimont
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    Modified for Velocity: one client per process, H.264 only, no audio,
    control or OpenGL filters, a key-frame request from the host, and the
    process exits when its client goes.

  The host side (crates/velocity-android/src/video.rs, mp4.rs) and the
  on-device animation guard (animations.rs) follow scrcpy's approach of a
  server started with `app_process` over `adb forward`; they are Velocity's
  own code.

